unning  a flame turret change our death by proxy  for wild fire to help spread the burn to  other targets  gear mod yuan a mixture of electronics  with skill hey store electronics with  skill power depending on the pieces  you're running you may need to have one  firearms mod to unlock your weapon  talents as far as the skill power to  skill haste ratio goes it depends on  your current overall skill haste the  maximum skill haste you can have is 50%  so anything over this is wasted get your  skill haste or as close to 50% as  possible and put the rest into skill  power be aware of skills like the mo  cache support station this adds 15  percent skill haste so if you are  running a support station build your  skill house shouldn't be above 35% you  can check your total skill haste plus a  large number of other things through the  character tab performance mods out of  youth damage dealing skills pick your  favorite this is the skill you'll be  further amplifying if it's your turret  turret damaged sticky bomb adds sticky  bomb damage in this example I'm using  seeker mind damage  as stated earlier sit back and let your  skills do and take the damage switch up  your skills depending on the mission if  you're having trouble with Russia's  running up to you and bursting you down  with shotguns or beating you with golf  clubs switch over to the flame turret it  can be hard in the heat of battle  but remember what weapon and ability  talents you have to increase your skill  damage finish off enemies with your  primary and remember to stack your  technicians bonus shoot down any turrets  and support stations and keep yourself  at full health where possible you're  squishy with this build but you can more  than make up for it with your damage  with this build you'll have success  soloing through challenging with ease  and even legendary missions the tricks  to legendary missions is knowing them  inside and out it's unlikely you'll  breeze through them without dying first  try but give them a few gos and you'll  start to remember the NPC types and  spawns these NPCs are tough but if you  can master these missions a lot of the  other content becomes a lot easier I've  also had a bit of success running  through resistance running up to wave 15  wasn't a problem but found greater  efficiency in opening the reward chest  three times by wave 10 and restarting  the NPC's started getting a little bit  tricky after that this is a good bill to  begin your farming for classified pieces  because this is a beginner's guide video  I haven't included any exotic gear apart  from the ninja bike messenger bag if you  manage to get a hold of the Barretts  bulletproof vest this is a great  addition to the build it'll give you a  further 10% increase of skill power on  the first skill you use skill power  builds can be a lot of fun and open a  lot more of the difficult content but  their lack of focus on survivability can  make them a little more tricky for the  newer player when things go wrong where  you get rushed down you do need to be  able to react quickly or you'll get  taken down fast play around with this  build and remember to adapt it to your  style of play hopefully this has given  you some good pointers or at least a  place to start  any further questions let me know next  we'll be covering the basic DPS build  and after that we'll have covered the  three most common build types that were  mentioned in part 1 so what videos would  you like to see next best farming  options for things like division tech or  Phoenix credits to help optimize your  builds more ninja bike builds maybe or  how to farm the dark zone solo if you  have any requests please mention them in  the comments and if the sound has  already mentioned to throw a thumbs up  otherwise thank you again for watching  this video and I'll see you in the next  Cheers  you  [Music]
 

